package "main"

// __c_global("sym", T) yields the ADDRESS of a C global as a raw *T, emitted
// verbatim (no name mangling).  POSIX `environ` has C type char** (Binate
// **char), so __c_global("environ", **char) is a ***char, and *it is the
// current **char — a null-terminated array of *char C strings.  This exercises
// the whole path: verbatim external data symbol + address-of-global + double
// deref (§16.9).  Positive counterpart to the negative VM-rejection test 983.
//
// Assert-internally "ok": there is always at least one environment entry when
// run normally, so a non-empty count confirms the recovered address is correct.
//
// Runs LIVE on every backend that has FFI: the LLVM modes, and — since §5b —
// all the native GOT modes (aarch64 Mach-O; x64 ELF + Mach-O), each reaching
// the real external `environ` GOT-indirect.  xfail only where the *environ
// example* can't run: the VM-interpreted modes (the bytecode VM does no FFI,
// by design) and both arm32-baremetal modes (no libc `environ` symbol to link
// against — arm32 native __c_global itself works via §5a; the example just has
// no baremetal definition).

func main() {
	var pp ***char = __c_global("environ", **char)
	var env **char = *pp
	var n int = 0
	for present(unsafe_index(env, n)) {
		n = n + 1
	}
	if n > 0 { println("ok") } else { println("FAIL") }
}
